*Visualizations, Code Snippets & Analytical Interpretations*

1 Distribution of Delivery Delays & SLA Adherence
Methodology & Visualization Rationale: A combined Histogram and Kernel Density Estimation (KDE) plot was selected to evaluate the probability distribution of lead-time variances against the zero-hour SLA threshold.

Key Analytical Insights: The delay distribution exhibits a distinct right-side tail (mean delay of +4.2 hours vs. median of +1.8 hours). Approximately 61.4% of total shipments meet on-time requirements (<=0 hours), while 38.6% violate promised customer delivery SLAs. Severe delays (>15 hours) constitute 11.2% of total consignments, identifying substantial tail risk in current operational scheduling.

# Visualization 1: Delay Distribution Plot
fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 3.8))
sns.histplot(df['Delay_Hours'], kde=True, color='#1B365D', bins=35, ax=ax)
