ax.set_title('Distribution of Delivery Delay Hours (Actual vs. Scheduled)', fontweight='bold')
ax.set_xlabel('Delay in Hours (<0 Early/On-time, >0 Late)')
ax.legend()
plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()

2 Transportation Cost Drivers (Distance, Mode & Volume)
Methodology & Visualization Rationale: A multi-dimensional scatter plot was constructed with color encoding for transport mode and point size representing cargo volume (m³) to assess multi-attribute cost behavior.

Key Analytical Insights: Distance is the primary linear driver of transportation costs, but modality exerts a strong multiplicative slope multiplier. Air Express displays the steepest marginal cost gradient ($5.50/KM/m³), whereas Rail Intermodal and Maritime Barge maintain shallow cost trajectories even at long ranges (>1,800 KM). Consignments exceeding 50 m³ volume incur significant penalty premiums when routed via Road Freight due to multi-truck dispatch requirements.


