3 Route Bottleneck Identification via Variance Dispersion
Methodology & Visualization Rationale: Boxplots were deployed to capture quartile dispersion, median transit variance, and outlier frequency across five primary shipping corridors.

Key Analytical Insights: The 'Trans-Mountain' and 'Pacific Coastal' corridors exhibit the highest median delays (+7.4h and +5.1h respectively) along with extended upper whiskers, demonstrating high operational instability and vulnerability to transit disruptions. In contrast, the 'Midwest Trunk' route maintains tight IQR bounds and low median delay (+0.6h), representing the most reliable operational corridor in the logistics network.

## Visualization 3: Route Bottleneck Boxplot
